# SelimBank.Api by hand. VS Code: "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then "Send Request" above each block.
# Visual Studio and Rider support .http files natively.
# The data is recreated on every start, so a blocked card becomes active again after a restart.

@host = http://localhost:7290
@customer = 1

### Demo customers (no header needed)
GET {{host}}/customers

### Accounts of the customer
GET {{host}}/accounts
X-Customer-Id: {{customer}}

### Last 5 transactions of account 1
GET {{host}}/accounts/1/transactions?take=5
X-Customer-Id: {{customer}}

### Cards (id and last 4 digits only)
GET {{host}}/cards
X-Customer-Id: {{customer}}

### Block card 1
POST {{host}}/cards/1/block
X-Customer-Id: {{customer}}

### Complaint about a transaction (182 is a card payment of customer 1; the seed is deterministic)
POST {{host}}/complaints
X-Customer-Id: {{customer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Bu harcamayı ben yapmadım.",
  "transactionId": 182
}

### 401: no header
GET {{host}}/accounts

### 404: customer 2 asks for customer 1's account
GET {{host}}/accounts/1/transactions
X-Customer-Id: 2
